From: Pyra kernel work <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: ti: aess: do not write uninitialised equaliser coefficients

aess_mixer_set_equ_profile() ends with

    src_coeff += profile * params.equ_length;
    memcpy(params.coef.type1, src_coeff, params.equ_length);
    omap_aess_write_filter(aess, id, &params);

coeff_data is only ever filled in by the topology loader. A firmware taken
through the legacy container path leaves every one NULL with profile_size
0, so the memcpy copies nothing into an uninitialised stack local and
write_filter() then copies a whole coefficient set out of it into CMEM.
Every equaliser -- DL1, DL2 left and right, sidetone, both mic filters --
ran on whatever happened to be on the stack.

With no coefficients to load, leave the ones the firmware image already
placed in CMEM. Found by inspection while chasing an audio quality problem;
it is a real defect either way, though it did not turn out to be the cause.
---
--- a/sound/soc/ti/aess/omap-aess-fw.c
+++ b/sound/soc/ti/aess/omap-aess-fw.c
@@ -468,6 +468,26 @@
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * coeff_data is only ever filled in by the topology loader
+	 * (aess_load_coeffs). A firmware loaded through the legacy container
+	 * path leaves every one of them NULL with profile_size 0, and the
+	 * code below then memcpy'd nothing into an uninitialised local and
+	 * handed that to omap_aess_write_filter(), which writes a whole
+	 * coefficient set from it into CMEM. The equalisers ended up running
+	 * on stack garbage -- an arbitrary filter, audible as a thin, tinny
+	 * tone against the direct McPDM link.
+	 *
+	 * With no coefficients to load, leave the ones the firmware image
+	 * already placed in CMEM alone.
+	 */
+	if (!src_coeff || !params.equ_length) {
+		dev_dbg(aess->dev,
+			"no equaliser coefficients for id %u, keeping the firmware's\n",
+			id);
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	src_coeff += profile * params.equ_length;
 	memcpy(params.coef.type1, src_coeff, params.equ_length);
 
